**RAG (Retrieval-Augmented Generation)** is an AI technique that combines external knowledge retrieval with the generative capabilities of large language models. By employing a two-stage "retrieve-then-generate" pipeline, RAG effectively addresses key limitations of traditional large models, such as outdated knowledge and hallucination issues. Its core advantages include: real-time knowledge updates (requiring only maintenance of the knowledge base), high answer reliability (grounded in authoritative sources), and controllable costs (eliminating the need for frequent model retraining). RAG is currently widely applied in scenarios such as intelligent customer service, knowledge-based question answering, research assistance, and enterprise document querying, making it one of the key technologies enabling practical deployment of large language models.
